meta {
  name: Create Invoice
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/invoices
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "partyType": "B2B",
    "sourceOrderIds": ["{{orderId}}"],
    "invoiceDueDate": "2026-09-15",
    "tdsDueDate": "2026-09-20",
    "isTdsApplicable": true,
    "tdsPercent": 10,
    "notes": "Consolidated monthly billing"
  }
}

docs {
  Create an invoice from selected outstanding order records. `partyType` is the
  Outstanding report panel (`B2B` / `REFERRED_BY` / `INTERNAL_REFERRAL_USER` /
  `EXTERNAL_REFERRAL_USER`). The server re-derives the gross amount (Σ of the
  orders' current outstanding due) and the party from `sourceOrderIds` — no amounts
  are read from the body. `isTdsApplicable`/`tdsPercent` are optional overrides
  (default from the party master). Errors: `INVOICE_ORDER_NOT_FOUND`,
  `INVOICE_ORDER_ALREADY_INVOICED` (409), `INVOICE_PARTY_MISMATCH`,
  `INVOICE_MIXED_PARTY`, `INVOICE_ORDER_NOT_OUTSTANDING`, `INVOICE_ZERO_AMOUNT`.
}
